    "q-81321": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81321",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{4}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}({y}^{4}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}{y}^{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}}{y}^{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
